**Definition 1.1 (original specimen, complete targets and error).** Let
$E:\mathbb C^3\to\mathbb C^5$ be the conditional calibrated isometry,
$P_V=EE^\dagger$, and

$$
\begin{aligned}
p_y&=(y/128,(64-y)/128,1/2),&
a_y&=(\sqrt{p_{y0}},\sqrt{p_{y1}},\sqrt{p_{y2}})^T,\\
U_{e,n}&=\operatorname{diag}(e,n,1),&
\rho_{y,e,n}&=U_{e,n}a_ya_y^TU_{e,n}^\dagger,\\
y&\in\{5,16,27\},&e,n&\in\{+1,-1\}.
\end{aligned}
\tag{EP.1}
$$

The sole input is one unknown normalized reached-old-live-cut specimen
$E\rho_{y,e,n}E^\dagger$. Its original height is $y/256$ and its winding
parity is $en=(-1)^m$. The ideal live target is the entire coherent
matrix $EU_{e,n}B_y^{\rm id}U_{e,n}^\dagger E^\dagger$, where
$B_y^{\rm id}$ is the conditional original matrix of CG.111 designated
in JR.1. Each of its coherent entries remains part of the target.
The five separate ideal failure measures, in the ORIGINAL label order
$\mathcal L=(0,1,2,3,13)$, are

$$
w_\ell f_y(t)dt\,P_f,\quad\ell\in\mathcal L,\qquad
(w_0,w_1,w_2,w_3,w_{13})=(0,1/4,1/2,1/4,0),\qquad
f_y(t)=\frac{6y}{(y+6t)^2},\quad 0\leq t\leq1.
\tag{EP.2}
$$

For the full ideal output $\Omega_{y,e,n}$ the error is

$$
E(\Phi)=\max_{y,e,n}\frac12
\|\Phi(E\rho_{y,e,n}E^\dagger)-\Omega_{y,e,n}\|_{1,\mathrm{cq}}.
\tag{EP.3}
$$

This is HALF the complete cq trace norm: coherent live entries, all
separately labelled Borel-time failure measures, singular components,
abort, wrong support, zero-ideal and extra sectors are counted. There is
no normalization by survival, acceptance or reached mass. The isolated
CG source point, exact ranks, normalization, coefficient enclosures,
endpoint witness saturation and minimax identification $E_*$ are named
conditional premises, as in JR. They are not recertified here.

